# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Express.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to dependencies
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json

### 2. Configured Analytics in HTML
- Modified `public/index.html` to include Vercel Web Analytics script
- Added the analytics initialization script in the `<head>` section
- Used the vanilla JavaScript/HTML implementation method as per official Vercel documentation

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the vanilla JavaScript approach suitable for this Express.js static site:

1. **Script Injection**: Added two script tags before the closing `</head>` tag:
   - Initialization script that sets up `window.va` function
   - Deferred loading of the analytics script from `/_vercel/insights/script.js`

2. **Framework Choice**: Since this is an Express.js backend serving static HTML files (not a React/Next.js/Vue application), the vanilla JavaScript implementation was the appropriate choice.

3. **Integration Method**: Used the recommended script tag approach for HTML/JavaScript projects, which:
   - Requires no build process
   - Works with static file serving
   - Automatically tracks page views when deployed to Vercel
   - Provides the `window.va()` API for custom event tracking if needed

## Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies (70 packages added)
- `public/index.html` - Added Vercel Analytics scripts to the head section

## Testing

- Verified package installation: `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1` installed successfully
- Confirmed Node.js syntax validation passes
- Verified HTML structure remains valid with analytics scripts added
- No linter configured in project, so no linting errors to check

## Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy this application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. After deployment, verify tracking is working by checking the browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section

## Notes

- The analytics will only function when deployed to Vercel
- Local development will not send analytics data
- The implementation follows Vercel's official documentation for vanilla JavaScript projects
- No additional configuration is needed in the Express.js server code
